since the equation is $(5x+ \frac {5}{x})-|4x- \frac {4}{x}|=m$,  
thus $5x+ \frac {5}{x}-4x+ \frac {4}{x}=m$, which simplifies to $x+ \frac {9}{x}=m$;  
since $x+ \frac {9}{x}\geqslant 6$;  
thus, when $m < 6$, the equation $x+ \frac {9}{x}=m$ has no solution;  
when $m=6$, the equation $x+ \frac {9}{x}=m$ has exactly one solution;  
when $6 < m < 10$, the equation $x+ \frac {9}{x}=m$ has two solutions in $(1,+\infty)$;  
